hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24376","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, who said: I heard Ziyad ibn Damrah ibn Sa'id al-Sulami narrating to Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father Damrah and from his grandfather, and both had witnessed Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in Dhuhr, then went to the shade of a tree and sat in it, while at Hunayn, then al-Aqra' ibn Habis and Uyaynah ibn Hisn ibn Hudhayfah ibn Badr came to him disputing about Amir ibn al-Adbat al-Ashja'i, and Uyaynah demanding the blood of Amir, while he was that day chief of Ghatafan, and al-Aqra' ibn Habis defending Muhallam ibn Jaththamah due to his place among Khindif, and they exchanged the dispute with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while we listened, and we heard Uyaynah saying: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I will not leave him until I make his women taste of grief what my women tasted, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Rather you take the blood-money, fifty in this journey of ours and fifty when we return, and he refused him, when a man of Banu Layth called Mukaytil, short and stocky, stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah I found for this slain no likeness in the beginning of Islam but as sheep that came to water, its first were shot and its last fled, lay a precedent today and change tomorrow, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raised his hand then said: Rather you take the blood-money, fifty in this journey of ours and fifty when we return, so they accepted the blood-money, then they said: Where is your companion, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, may seek forgiveness for him, so a brown thin tall man stood, with a suit he had prepared in it for killing, until he sat before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: What is your name, he said: I am Muhallam ibn Jaththamah, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raised his hand then said: O Allah, do not forgive Muhallam ibn Jaththamah, so he stood wiping his tears with the edge of his cloak, as for us among ourselves, we say: We hope the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sought forgiveness for him, but what appeared from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is this."
